# Grammar guide images (Unsplash)

## No accidental reuse across guides

- Each grammar guide that uses Unsplash should keep its own `*-images.generated.ts` (or equivalent) module.
- **Do not reuse the same `unsplashId` in another grammar guide** unless the repetition is **intentional** (for example a deliberate cross-reference learners should recognize) or **strictly necessary** for clarity. When reusing, add a short comment next to the entry (or in the fetch script) explaining why.
- When adding or refetching images for one guide, treat **every other guide’s `unsplashId` values as reserved**. Prefer extending the relevant `fetch-*.ts` script so the Unsplash picker seeds `usedPhotoIds` from other generated modules (see `fetch-reported-speech-images.ts` and `medical-instructions-images.generated.ts`).
- After edits, ensure **no duplicate `unsplashId` strings** appear across `src/data/*-images.generated.ts` except where documented as intentional.

## Attribution

- Keep `credit.name`, `credit.url`, `unsplashPage`, and `alt` accurate and learner-appropriate when swapping photos.
